 files created during installation were not shown removed; both are treated as retained, low-risk residue. Final lifecycle observations show healthy package state, no failed services, no bootstrap listener, and only the expected Redis/Sentinel cache-network sockets.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b4266cddd77945f6","cmd-d7a0049b1e8c45f5","cmd-0cf869fba6d64358","cmd-2855da72896740e1","cmd-5a7ad83264ef498f","cmd-1880c7da4a79446a","cmd-9d77ef6f9ebd48be","cmd-54b2ac188c6a43ff","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The captured transition proves initial node1 leadership, automatic failover with continued writes, and synchronized recovery of node1. The independent restart protocol is complete for every node: each has a healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service, data, and Sentinel state. The fixed lifecycle boot identities agree with those transitions. Only minor evidence/install-file residue affects hygiene.","limitations":["No explicit plaintext connection attempt against Sentinel 26379 was captured; Sentinel's TLS-only assessment instead combines successful live TLS commands, client-certificate rejection, port 0/tls-port configuration, and the observed listener.","The lifecycle inventory covers /tmp, sockets, failed units, package health, and boot identity, but not /root or /var/log; retention of the preboot markers and custom installation logs is inferred from their creation and the absence of cleanup in the complete command trace.","The lifecycle collector did not independently perform authenticate